WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.756 --> 00:00:15.229
Pedro zigzagged around Great-Aunt Luisa's dark front yard, holding his phone up.

2
00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:18.328
He was trying to get a stronger signal.

3
00:00:18.329 --> 00:00:24.750
Great-Aunt Luisa lived in the countryside, where there wasn't much to do.

4
00:00:24.751 --> 00:00:30.525
Pedro was staying with her for a whole month.

5
00:00:30.526 --> 00:00:35.120
"Are you taking pictures of the moon?" a voice called.

6
00:00:35.121 --> 00:00:38.955
Pedro spotted a girl in a neighbor's yard.

7
00:00:38.956 --> 00:00:41.696
"No. I was just trying to get a signal."

8
00:00:41.697 --> 00:00:43.946
He glanced upward.

9
00:00:43.947 --> 00:00:49.438
The nearly full moon looked much brighter than it looked at home in the city.

10
00:00:49.439 --> 00:00:56.519
The girl smiled. "I'm Luna. Want to take a look through my telescope?"

11
00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:02.969
"Sure." Pedro walked over to where Luna had set up her telescope.

12
00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:06.597
"I've never seen the moon through a telescope before."

13
00:01:06.598 --> 00:01:13.344
"One day I'd like to see it up close." Luna's eyes shone.

14
00:01:13.345 --> 00:01:18.818
"My dream is to become an astronaut and explore the moon."

15
00:01:18.819 --> 00:01:21.313
"You sure like the moon a lot.

16
00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:26.826
Is it because your name means 'moon' in Spanish?" Pedro asked teasingly.

17
00:01:26.827 --> 00:01:30.241
Luna grinned. "It could be.

18
00:01:30.242 --> 00:01:33.649
Hey! There's a full moon tomorrow.

19
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:36.485
Want to watch it with me?"

20
00:01:36.486 --> 00:01:41.129
Pedro smiled. "Definitely!"

21
00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:46.626
The next night Pedro met Luna in her yard.

22
00:01:46.627 --> 00:01:50.486
"The moon is a different shape tonight," he said.

23
00:01:50.487 --> 00:01:56.320
Luna giggled. "The moon doesn't really change shape, you know.

24
00:01:56.321 --> 00:01:59.612
The sun lights up the moon's surface.

25
00:01:59.613 --> 00:02:06.468
As the moon orbits around Earth, the amount of the sunlit surface we can see changes.

26
00:02:06.469 --> 00:02:10.009
These changes are the phases of the moon."

27
00:02:10.010 --> 00:02:12.755
"Aha," Pedro said.

28
00:02:12.756 --> 00:02:16.821
"How long does it take for the moon to orbit Earth?"

29
00:02:16.822 --> 00:02:21.919
"About four weeks—one lunar month," Luna said.

30
00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.235
"Oh. Is tonight the start of a lunar month?"

31
00:02:26.236 --> 00:02:32.469
"Nope! The full moon is halfway through a lunar month," Luna explained.

32
00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:36.174
"The new moon is the start of a lunar month.

33
00:02:36.175 --> 00:02:39.137
But it's a confusing name."

34
00:02:39.138 --> 00:02:41.720
"Why?" Pedro asked.

35
00:02:41.721 --> 00:02:46.281
"Because that's when the unlit surface of the moon is facing Earth.

36
00:02:46.282 --> 00:02:49.456
We can't see the moon then."

37
00:02:49.457 --> 00:02:54.245
"That should be called a 'no moon' then!" Pedro grinned.

38
00:02:54.246 --> 00:03:03.226
Luna laughed. "After a new moon, the moon waxes—or looks like it gets bigger.

39
00:03:03.227 --> 00:03:07.102
A few days later, it's a waxing crescent.

40
00:03:07.103 --> 00:03:11.878
One week after the new moon is the first-quarter moon.

41
00:03:11.879 --> 00:03:17.677
That's when half of the moon's surface is visible from Earth."

42
00:03:17.678 --> 00:03:21.945
"Why is it a quarter moon if half of it is visible?"

43
00:03:21.946 --> 00:03:27.290
"Because it's one quarter of the way through the lunar month," Luna said.

44
00:03:27.291 --> 00:03:32.638
"Finally after another week, we have a full moon, like this one.

45
00:03:32.639 --> 00:03:34.834
Are you enjoying it?"

46
00:03:34.835 --> 00:03:38.316
Pedro put his eye to the telescope again.

47
00:03:38.317 --> 00:03:47.072
"It's awesome!"

48
00:03:47.073 --> 00:03:54.414
For the next few nights, Pedro and Luna watched the moon slowly seem to disappear.

49
00:03:54.415 --> 00:04:02.011
"It's waning. This is a waning gibbous," Luna explained, pointing to the football-shaped moon.

50
00:04:02.012 --> 00:04:06.154
"In a few days, we'll see the third-quarter moon."

51
00:04:06.155 --> 00:04:11.840
Over a week later it was a new moon, and the sky was moonless.

52
00:04:11.841 --> 00:04:18.078
Soon the moon reappeared, and the waxing moon slowly grew again.

53
00:04:18.079 --> 00:04:26.603
One night, under a full moon, Pedro's mom arrived to pick him up.

54
00:04:26.604 --> 00:04:32.163
"Hey, Pedro!" Luna called as Pedro put his stuff into Mom's car.

55
00:04:32.164 --> 00:04:36.242
Luna was holding a big, long box.

56
00:04:36.243 --> 00:04:38.900
"I thought you might like this."

57
00:04:38.901 --> 00:04:43.032
"Whoa! I can't take that," Pedro said.

58
00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:45.349
It was her telescope!

59
00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:47.618
Luna grinned.

60
00:04:47.619 --> 00:04:50.099
"I'm getting a new one soon.

61
00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:54.286
So please take this one."

62
00:04:54.287 --> 00:04:57.151
"Thanks!" Pedro said.

63
00:04:57.152 --> 00:04:59.824
"That's really generous, Luna.

64
00:04:59.825 --> 00:05:03.405
I'm sorry that I don't have anything for you though."

65
00:05:03.406 --> 00:05:07.052
"That's okay." Luna smiled.

66
00:05:07.053 --> 00:05:12.044
"Just promise me we can moon-gaze together when I visit the city."

67
00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:21.177
Pedro smiled back. "Deal!"
